            {
                "content": "# TULARE LAKE BASIN (cont.)\n\nEXTREMES OF DISCHARGE.-Maximum stage during year, from water-stage re- corder, 4.58 feet at 6.30 p. m. May 26 (discharge, 680 second-feet); mini- mum stage, 1.44 feet from 5 to 7 p. m. October 1 (discharge, 0.4 second-foot). 1921-1925: Maximum stage recorded, 5.02 feet at 8 p. m. June 4, 1922 (discharge, 870 second-feet); minimum stage recorded, 1.38 feet part of September 12-14, 1924 (discharge, 0.3 second-foot).\n\nDIVERSIONS.-None.\n\nREGULATION.-None\n\nICE.-Float frozen in ice in well December 17 to March 17. ACcuRAcY.-Stage-discharge relation permanent. Rating curve well defined. Water-stage recorder record excellent. Daily discharge ascertained by apply- ing mean daily gage height to rating table. Discharge estimated Decem- ber 17 to March 17 in monthly table. Records good.\n\nCOOPERATION.-Gage-height record and results of discharge measurements fur- nished by San Joaquin Light & Power Corporation.\n\nDischarge measurements of North Fork of Kings River below Meadow Brook, Calif., during the year ending September 30, 1925",
